# carcommunity environment configuration
#
# No code in the live stacks (functions/, apps/admin, apps/android, scripts/)
# reads a root-level .env file. Environment configuration lives with the
# stack that consumes it:
#
# - Admin web portal (Vite): apps/admin/.env.example
#   Copy to apps/admin/.env.local and fill in values.
#
# - Cloud Functions runtime config: functions/.env (Firebase CLI convention,
#   git-ignored). Currently the only manually configured variable sourced
#   from functions/.env is:
#     EARLY_MEMBER_CUTOFF_DATE  ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD) for the early_member
#                               badge cutoff; unset = badge not awarded.
#   (The functions code also reads platform-provided variables such as
#   FUNCTIONS_EMULATOR, GCLOUD_PROJECT, and *_EMULATOR_HOST, which are set
#   automatically by the Firebase runtime/emulators — never configure those
#   by hand.)
#
# - Cloud Functions secrets: managed in Google Cloud Secret Manager, never in
#   .env files. Set with `firebase functions:secrets:set <NAME>`.
#     GITHUB_ISSUE_TOKEN  token used by the diagnostics/feedback functions to
#                         open GitHub issues.
#
# - scripts/set-first-admin.mjs reads FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID (or
#   GCLOUD_PROJECT / GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT) and CONFIRM=1 from the shell
#   environment; see the header of that script.
#
# Never commit real values or .env files to version control.
